WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.075
Three more things before you inspect.

2
00:00:02.075 --> 00:00:06.918
The privacy scope: Learn auto-creates
a system bypass rule for incompatible

3
00:00:06.918 --> 00:00:11.300
destinations, and an editable
recommended bypass for the Education,

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.913
Finance, Government, and Health
and Medicine categories.

5
00:00:14.913 --> 00:00:19.072
The guide keeps them, adds the
categories the privacy officer names,

6
00:00:19.072 --> 00:00:22.787
and records the scope in the
system's privacy documentation.

7
00:00:22.787 --> 00:00:25.901
Learn says to establish
and communicate a T

8
00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:29.100
L S policy to users
before inspection starts.

9
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.588
Pinned applications fail under inspection;

10
00:00:31.588 --> 00:00:34.747
Learn's answer is a custom
bypass for their destinations,

11
00:00:34.747 --> 00:00:36.832
without duplicating the system list,

12
00:00:36.832 --> 00:00:41.000
and developer tools with their own
certificate stores need the root added.

13
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.506
And the failure line:
Microsoft's recommendation treats

14
00:00:44.506 --> 00:00:47.862
a failure rate above one
percent as a systemic problem.

15
00:00:47.862 --> 00:00:55.862
Inspection doesn't negotiate H T T P two,
and doesn't follow A I A or O C S P links.

16
00:00:55.862 --> 00:01:00.126
Learn's pages give the T L S status
values differently in two places,

17
00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:04.700
so group by what your workspace
actually holds before writing an alert.

18
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.063
Where are agencies?

19
00:01:06.063 --> 00:01:11.526
Internet Access and T L S inspection need
an Internet Access or Suite license,

20
00:01:11.526 --> 00:01:15.624
and are available in G C C by
Learn's product-wide statement.

21
00:01:15.624 --> 00:01:20.674
The cloud firewall for clients and the
Explicit Forward Proxy are preview,

22
00:01:20.674 --> 00:01:23.900
and their G C C availability
isn't yet specified.
